    <string name="setup_auth_gmail">Gmail needs an app password: with 2-Step Verification on, make one at myaccount.google.com/apppasswords and type it in Password. It replaces your Gmail password here: nothing to turn off.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_icloud">iCloud needs an app-specific password: make one at account.apple.com, Sign-In and Security, App-Specific Passwords, and type it in Password. It replaces your Apple Account password here and works with two-factor authentication.</string>
    <!-- What each provider asks of another app (docs/MAIL.md §11; D for the words). -->
    <string name="setup_auth_yahoo">Yahoo needs an app password: at login.yahoo.com/account/security, Generate app password, then type it in Password. It replaces your Yahoo password here and works with two-step verification: nothing to turn off.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_aol">AOL needs an app password: at login.aol.com/account/security, Generate app password, then type it in Password. It replaces your AOL password here and works with two-step verification: nothing to turn off.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_gmx">GMX lets other apps in once IMAP is on: on GMX\'s website (gmx.net, gmx.com, gmx.fr…), Email Settings, POP3/IMAP, allow POP3 and IMAP access. With two-factor authentication on, type an app password made in GMX\'s security settings: it replaces your password here.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_webde">WEB.DE lets other apps in once IMAP is on: at web.de, Email Settings, POP3/IMAP, allow POP3 and IMAP access. With two-factor authentication on, type an app password made in WEB.DE\'s security settings: it replaces your password here.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_mailcom">mail.com lets other apps in with a Premium account only, once POP3 and IMAP access is on in mail.com\'s Email Settings. With two-factor authentication on, type an app password: it replaces your password here.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_zoho">Zoho Mail lets other apps in once IMAP Access is on: Settings, Mail Accounts, IMAP. With two-factor authentication on, type an app-specific password from accounts.zoho.com, Security, App Passwords: it replaces your password here.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_yandex">Yandex needs an app password: at id.yandex.com/security/app-passwords, create one for Mail and type it in Password. In Yandex Mail, Settings, Email clients, turn on IMAP first.</string>
    <string name="setup_auth_orange">Orange needs its password for email apps: in your Espace Client, Connexion et sécurité, Logiciels, generate it and type it in Password. POP and IMAP access must be on in Mail Orange\'s settings.</string>
    <string name="setup_outlook_browser">Outlook.com, Hotmail and Live addresses sign in through the browser only: Microsoft refuses passwords in other apps since September 16, 2024. Select Sign In With Browser.</string>
    <string name="setup_outlook_off">Outlook.com, Hotmail and Live addresses sign in through the browser only (Microsoft refuses passwords in other apps since September 16, 2024), and browser sign-in is off in this build of Bold7. This address cannot be set up yet.</string>
    <string name="setup_work_account">This address is a Microsoft 365 work or school account. Microsoft takes no password from other apps, and browser sign-in here is for personal accounts only: it cannot be set up yet.</string>
    <string name="setup_proton">Proton Mail reaches other email apps only through Proton Mail Bridge, on a computer. It cannot be set up on this smartphone.</string>
